.TH SDL_SeekIO 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SeekIO \- Seek within an
.BR SDL_IOStream
data stream.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_iostream.h>
.PP
.BI "Sint64 SDL_SeekIO(SDL_IOStream *context, Sint64 offset, SDL_IOWhence whence);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function seeks to byte
.BR offset ,
relative to
.BR whence \[char46]
.PP
.BR whence
may be any of the following values:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_IO_SEEK_SET :
seek from the beginning of data
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_IO_SEEK_CUR :
seek relative to current read point
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_IO_SEEK_END :
seek relative to the end of data
.PP
If this stream can not seek, it will return -1\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I context
a pointer to an
.BR SDL_IOStream
structure\[char46]
.TP
.I offset
an offset in bytes, relative to
.BR whence
location; can be negative\[char46]
.TP
.I whence
any of
.BR SDL_IO_SEEK_SET ,
.BR SDL_IO_SEEK_CUR ,
.BR SDL_IO_SEEK_END \[char46]

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the final offset in the data stream after the seek or -1 on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
Do not use the same
.BR SDL_IOStream
from two threads at once\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_TellIO (3)
